  "answers": [
    "Here's the preview. Nothing has been deleted yet.\n\n**If you confirm, this will:**\n1. Remove the Google tokens stored locally.\n2. Cancel any active Google jobs.\n3. Permanently delete the local Google records and the raw API responses kept on this machine.\n\n**This will not:**\n- Delete your Takeout data. It stays in place.\n- Revoke the app's access on Google's side. The authorization stays active at Google.\n\nBecause the local tokens are removed, the app can't pull new Google data until you reconnect. Reconnecting would reuse the existing Google authorization.\n\nThe deletion is permanent, and this confirmation expires in 5 minutes. Do you want me to proceed? Reply \"yes\" to confirm.",
    "The local Google data has been deleted. Takeout data was kept, and remote access was not revoked.\n\n- **Local Google records:** 3 records deleted.\n- **Raw response files:** none were found to delete.\n- **Local tokens:** none were stored, so there was nothing to remove.\n- **Takeout data:** kept.\n- **Google authorization:** still active on Google's side.\n\nMy first attempt to apply the deletion failed because the confirmation had expired. I requested a new preview, which listed the same three actions, and applied it. You may want to check the status of the Google connection, since the app has no local tokens now and would need to reconnect to pull new Google data."
